# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context filter.
#
# The build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (see docker-compose.yml -> build.context: ..),
# because the Dockerfile lives in deployment/ but needs backend/ sources. Everything
# below is either build output, an IDE artefact, a secret, or the Flutter app — none of
# which belong in a backend image. Keeping the context small is not cosmetic: every byte
# here is tarred and shipped to the daemon on every build, and any file that changes
# invalidates the COPY layer that includes it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- VCS / CI -------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Gradle & Java build output ------------------------------------------
# backend/bin is Eclipse/Buildship output (see CLAUDE.md); never ship it.
**/build/
**/bin/
**/.gradle/
**/out/
**/*.class
**/*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
**/*.war

# --- IDE ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.idea/
**/.settings/
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/*.iml
**/.vscode/

# --- Secrets: must never enter an image layer ----------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.jks

# --- The Flutter app is not part of the backend image --------------------
owner_app/

# --- Deployment assets are bind-mounted at runtime, not baked in ---------
deployment/

# --- Docs, logs, scratch --------------------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md
**/*.log
**/logs/
**/backups/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
